Reset CommandInformation at audio session ownership boundaries

The hub retains supported_commands_plist after a session ends, and D-Bus
leaves CommandInformation unchanged when the plist is NULL. Free and clear
the plist, notify watchers, and publish an empty av to disable stale AP2
controls. A fresh supported-commands update can then re-enable the same
capabilities, including when reconnecting from the same sender.

Reset synchronously when get_play_lock acquires a different audio
connection, and when release_play_lock or stop_play releases it. Do not
reset in the queued conn handler: /command updates the hub synchronously
and can overtake queued metadata. Already-owned connections and RC-only
SETUP must not reset controls. Neither pend (also emitted for stream-only
TEARDOWN and stream replacement) nor disc (also emitted by RC event
receivers) is a reliable audio session boundary. Pausing, resuming and
replacing streams within the same connection must retain capabilities.

Rebased for 94070a1d514229b03a1ca202297a20a8993d6d92 (5.6-dev).

--- a/metadata/hub.c
+++ b/metadata/hub.c
@@ -129,5 +129,19 @@
 void metadata_hub_stop(void) {}
 
+void metadata_hub_reset_session_commands(void) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_AIRPLAY_2
+  // Called synchronously at audio ownership changes, not from queued conn/pend metadata.
+  int changed = 0;
+  metadata_hub_modify_prolog();
+  if (metadata_store.supported_commands_plist != NULL) {
+    plist_free(metadata_store.supported_commands_plist);
+    metadata_store.supported_commands_plist = NULL;
+    changed = 1;
+  }
+  metadata_hub_modify_epilog(changed);
+#endif
+}
+
 void add_metadata_watcher(metadata_watcher fn) {
   int i;
   for (i = 0; i < number_of_watchers; i++) {
